# The tagged group across selections of one object (spec 06 §2.5, §2.8; the accuracy pass of
# 2026-10-15), on a training game of our own (tests/input/learn-moves): turn-based, two attack
# ships at home.
# - Only Shift+C and a sector's selection clear the tags: a Goto that selects one ship elsewhere
#   (here Ships\Units' row) keeps them, its report shows with OpenSE4's line saying the next
#   order goes to the tagged group, and that order goes to the tagged ship, not to the one shown.
# - OpenSE4's option "Clear tags when selecting a ship elsewhere" (Options, OpenSE4) clears them
#   then, as OpenSE4 did before.
# (docs/BUILDING.md "Input scripts")
# layouts: both (also plays at 800x600: run_input_tests.py --small)
options --learn-dir=tests/input/learn-moves --training=moves --layout=1024x768 --size=1280x800

wait-lesson moves
wait 5
click tag:lesson:hide
# The first ship sets out for the far corner: it stands elsewhere afterwards.
click sector:home
wait-for item:report:ship
click item:"California 0001*"
wait 2
key M
wait-until { picking = "move-to" }
click sector:12,12
wait-gone sector:gliding

# OpenSE4's option on: the Goto to the first ship clears the tags.
key F2
wait-window game-menu
click item:Options in=game-menu
wait-window options
click item:"Clear tags when selecting a ship elsewhere" in=options
key Escape
wait-closed options
click sector:home
wait-for item:report:ship
click item:"California 0002*" shift
wait-for item:tagged:1
key F6
wait-window ships
click item:##row in=ships nth=1
wait-closed ships
wait 2
assert-present item:Comps
assert-absent item:tagged:*

# The original's rule (the option off again): the tags stay through the Goto.
key F2
wait-window game-menu
click item:Options in=game-menu
wait-window options
click item:"Clear tags when selecting a ship elsewhere" in=options
key Escape
wait-closed options
click sector:home
wait-for item:report:ship
click item:"California 0002*" shift
wait-for item:tagged:1
key F6
wait-window ships
click item:##row in=ships nth=1
wait-closed ships
wait 2
# The first ship's report, with the line that the next order goes to the tagged ship.
assert-present item:Comps
assert-present item:tagged:1
assert-absent sector:home+selected
screenshot tags-kept.png
# Move To: given to the tagged ship at home, not to the one shown.
key M
wait-until { picking = "move-to" }
click sector:0,0
wait 5
assert { command = "OrderTagged" }
assert-absent item:tagged:*
wait-gone sector:gliding
# The home sector holds the colony alone now: the tagged ship left (the one shown had no
# movement left).
click sector:home
wait 3
assert-absent item:report:ship
